' session: e2da2921-e414-40e8-bb19-8b3ea51c1aad
'
' ── WHAT THIS FILE IS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A decision record. It carries no `covers:` and is no source file's SPEC
' pointer (_refactors/ is exempt from the referencing rule). The current
' state lives in:
'   mise tasks + the two mains ...... _spec/cmd/proveo/usage.puml
'   lint + post-commit hook ......... _spec/_devops/git-hooks.puml
'   unit baseline ................... _spec/_devops/unit-baseline.puml
'   release gate · idle · ladder .... _spec/_devops/release-gate.puml
'   release + CDN staging ........... _spec/internal/cdn/distribution-update.puml
'   image fleet ..................... _spec/internal/maintain/image-build-deploy.puml
'   host-shell allowlist + argv rule  _spec/tests/20-contract.puml
' It SUPERSEDES P4 decision 2 of the frozen _spec/_refactors/host-shell-to-go.puml
' ("maintainer tooling lives in cmd/proveo-dev, a separate binary that never
' ships"). That file stays untouched.
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── THE GOAL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The operator, 2026-11-12: "proveo-dev should have been completely replaced
' by mise". Before: 29 files under cmd/proveo-dev (2,151 source lines, 900
' test lines, the 18-line unit-baseline.txt), a cobra root reached by 17 of
' 24 mise tasks, and a POSIX post-commit shim that exec'd it.
'
' ── THE OPTIONS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' C  CHOSEN. Every thin wrapper becomes a native mise task (run arrays,
'    depends, usage args and flags, env, per-task tools). Every gate verdict
'    moves into the Go test it gates, so go test's exit code is the verdict.
'    Upstream tools absorb the rest: mise generate git-pre-commit, goreleaser,
'    go tool covdata, golangci-lint fmt, go test -skip, mise run
'    --continue-on-error. Two producer package mains remain, both under
'    internal/: CDN staging (internal/cdn/stage over goreleaser's dist
'    metadata) and the image fleet (internal/maintain/fleet over
'    internal/maintain + internal/imagebuild).
' A  NOT CHOSEN: one internal/devtask runner keyed on MISE_TASK_NAME. It is
'    the dispatcher under a new name.
' B  NOT CHOSEN: one main per tool. It moves ~1,400 lines verbatim, keeps the
'    text-parsing gates and keeps the stage-cdn defects.
' D  NOT CHOSEN: mise-native with sh one-liners. It reintroduces host shell
'    logic, which the 2026-09-22 rule removed.
'
' ── OPERATOR CHOICES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' 1 VERSION. With no -X main.version stamp, cmd/proveo reports
'   dev@<12 hex of vcs.revision>, plus "+dirty" when vcs.modified, from Go
'   build info (cmd/proveo/version.go). goreleaser's -X still wins. go run
'   stamps no build info and reports dev. TestBuiltBinaryReportsItsVersion
'   builds cmd/proveo twice and reads --version.
' 2 DEPLOY-CLI. Tag only. An untagged HEAD refuses with one line naming the
'   fix (TestReleaseShipsATaggedHead under PROVEO_RELEASE_GATE=1, before
'   goreleaser runs). No snapshot deploys to the production CDN. dev-cli
'   stays a local snapshot preview.
' 3 RENDER-SUBAGENTS. Deleted: code, tests, references. The operator: "in the
'   future this will likely print out a template".
'
' ── EXECUTOR DEFAULTS (each with what was NOT CHOSEN) ──────────────────────
' * Four work packages: gates, cli and images rewired mise.toml and landed
'   each replacement with the contract pins of the lines they changed; the
'   dispatcher stayed compiled but unreached until cleanup deleted it whole
'   (render-subagents went in images, operator choice 3). NOT CHOSEN:
'   deleting each replaced verb file in its own package (the unused linter
'   flags the orphaned shared helpers); deferring every contract rewrite to
'   cleanup (the first three packages would land red).
' * SKIP_GIT_HOOKS keeps its name through post-commit's skip_if with
'   envflag's on-words (TestPostCommitSkipIfSpeaksTheEnvflagWords).
'   NOT CHOSEN: MISE_TASK_SKIP=post-commit (renames the switch);
'   skip_if = 'test -n "$SKIP_GIT_HOOKS"' (shell logic, and 0 would skip);
'   editing the generated hook (untracked, regenerated).
' * The race fallback is a usage flag --no-race on test-go and baseline.
'   NOT CHOSEN: a Tera exec() race probe (it renders with the caller's PATH,
'   not the task's tools); dropping the fallback with no flag.
' * test-e2e-full keeps going after a red half through a nested `mise run
'   --continue-on-error e2e-gated … ::: idle-all ::: ladder-all`, ordered by
'   wait_for; its own args reach the e2e pass alone. NOT CHOSEN: one go test
'   process for all halves (a timeout panic aborts the rest); depends_post
'   ([Unverified] exit status on a red parent); a run array (stops at the
'   first failure); raw_args (passes --help to go test).
' * The two mains live at internal/cdn/stage and internal/maintain/fleet,
'   where the env-registry scan already looks. NOT CHOSEN: internal/devtool/*
'   (a namespace with no library beside it); tools/ (the scan must learn it);
'   cmd/ (reads as a shipped binary).
' * PROVEO_LADDER_TARGET stays singular: four hidden ladder:<def> tasks keep
'   one 30m process per def, and ladder-all runs them with
'   --continue-on-error --jobs=1. NOT CHOSEN:
'   PROVEO_LADDER_TARGETS with a subtest loop in one 120m process.
' * PROVEO_COV_DIR, PROVEO_CDN_ROOT, PROVEO_DIST_DIR and
'   PROVEO_CDN_REQUIRE_DIST retire with the Go that read them; no tracked
'   file sets them. PROVEO_VERSION stays, read by install.sh and install.ps1
'   only. Every other env name stays.
' * --print stays on build, deploy and test-defs (the fleet main), because
'   `mise run -n` shows only the fleet line there. It goes from idle, ladder
'   and e2e-full. Their go test lines print with `mise run -n e2e-gated`,
'   `mise run -n idle-all` and `mise run -n ladder:<def>`; `mise run -n
'   ladder-all` and `test-e2e-full` print only the nested `mise run` line.
'   `mise tasks info <task>` prints the env, PROVEO_IDLE_FOR as its
'   unrendered template; idle-all's description names the 45s default.
'   NOT CHOSEN: --print everywhere (a Go wrapper per gate); --print nowhere
'   (loses the wave plan).
' * build, deploy and test-defs share one fleet main (verbs build|deploy|test).
'   test-defs keeps all and --print and runs each distinct suite once.
'   NOT CHOSEN: test-defs as a direct `go test -run=^TestImage<Suite>$`;
'   three claudecode reruns under all.
' * build, deploy and test-defs require <target>; the DNS help and the image
'   suites' not-built skip name `mise run build <target>`. NOT CHOSEN:
'   default="all" (a bare build would build 13 images); an optional target.
' * mise.toml joins the env-registry scan as an envreg.Binary reader. NOT
'   CHOSEN: a new Where bit (changes `proveo help env` for no operator gain).
' * Contract tests read mise.toml through a small hand-written reader. NOT
'   CHOSEN: a TOML module in go.mod; shelling out to mise in unit tests.
' * The gofmt gate is TestEveryTrackedGoFileIsGofmted (go/format over git
'   ls-files), first in lint. NOT CHOSEN: golangci-lint formatters alone
'   (they miss build-constrained files); a gofmt -l run entry (needs shell).
' * Opted-in e2e gates fail their skips through failSkipsWhenOptedIn, a
'   t.Cleanup + t.Skipped helper (e2e/gate_test.go) installed first in
'   TestSandboxLadder (after its opt-out) and idleAtPrompt; the release
'   ledger uses the same pattern. NOT CHOSEN: a gateSkip helper replacing
'   each t.Skip (misses future bare skips).
' * The untagged-HEAD refusal is TestReleaseShipsATaggedHead inside
'   release-ledger. NOT CHOSEN: goreleaser's own refusal (names no fix); a
'   Tera exec() tag probe (renders with the outer PATH).
' * confirm guards deploy-cli only. NOT CHOSEN: confirm on deploy (an empty
'   templated confirm still prompts, so scripted deploys would need --yes).
' * build-cli sets env GOBIN = false, so go install writes to its own
'   GOPATH/bin. A `go env -w GOBIN=…` entry still wins over it (MEASURED);
'   HEAD's explicit GOPATH/bin overrode that entry. NOT CHOSEN: GOBIN from
'   get_env(GOPATH) (misses go env -w GOPATH); GOBIN from exec() (outer
'   PATH); GOENV=off (also drops GOPRIVATE and GOPROXY); [settings]
'   go.set_gobin (absent here).
' * An operator env value reaches a task through `{% set v = get_env(name=…,
'   default='') | trim %}{% if v %}…{% else %}<default>{% endif %}`, so an
'   empty or blank value falls back like HEAD's envOr did
'   (TestOperatorEnvTreatsEmptyAsUnset). NOT CHOSEN: get_env's own default
'   (it applies only to an unset variable, so `-timeout` lost its value).
' * Every {{ … }} in a run string ends in `| quote`, so a --tag, a path with a
'   space or an env value reaches argv as one word; boolean flags render
'   through {% if %} as bare -no-cache and -print. NOT CHOSEN: `| as_str |
'   quote` on booleans (quote refuses a bool); quoting only free-form values
'   (the scan cannot tell them apart).
' * The plain-argv scan is an allowlist: outside '…' and Tera blocks a run
'   string holds letters, digits, space and -_./=:,@+%^, a $ only at a word's
'   end, and starts with a program, not a bash keyword, builtin or env. The scan
'   also refuses task forms it cannot read: a [tasks] shorthand, a top-level
'   tasks. key, a task sub-table and a key outside its list (run_windows,
'   file, shell). NOT CHOSEN: extending the denylist (the next construct
'   slips through); calling mise to render tasks (needs mise in unit tests).
' * The fallback version is dev@<12 hex>[+dirty]. NOT CHOSEN: 7 or 8 hex
'   (git's abbrev varies by repo size); an unstamped dev.
' * internal/cdn/stage reads its platforms from .goreleaser.yaml
'   builds[id=proveo] and checks each binary against goreleaser's checksum.
'   NOT CHOSEN: a hard-coded 8-platform list; jq or sh one-liners.
' * The unit baseline is one backslash-continued string in mise.toml [vars].
'   NOT CHOSEN: a TOML array ([vars] rejects arrays); one 700-column line;
'   keeping unit-baseline.txt (it lived in the deleted directory).
' * ci is depends-only; test-images moves its assignment into an env table.
'   NOT CHOSEN: keeping the non-ASCII printf (fails the plain-argv rule).
' * choiceui FilterList.Multi is deleted in cleanup, with its one caller.
'   NOT CHOSEN: deleting it while maintain.go still compiled against it.
' * _spec/_plans/repo-simplification.puml keeps its dated rows under one
'   history header line; living specs carry no literal dispatcher name; one
'   pointer line in usage.puml names this record. NOT CHOSEN: rewriting 21
'   dated findings; freezing the whole plan (11 rows are still OPEN).
'
' ── THE VERB MAP ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   lint · commentlint · gofmt -l ... [tasks.lint]: TestEveryTrackedGoFileIsGofmted
'                                     + TestNoCommentBlockOverThreeLines, go vet
'                                     (default, image, e2e), golangci-lint run
'   hooks install ................. install-git-hooks: mise generate
'                                     git-pre-commit --hook post-commit
'   hooks post-commit ............. hidden post-commit: {fmt}, {lint}, skip_if
'   baseline + unit-baseline.txt .. baseline: go test -skip over [vars]
'   coverage unit · merge · e2e ... test-go (cov/unit) · coverage (covdata) ·
'                                     test-go-e2e / test-e2e
'   coverage all .................. deleted; `mise run -c test-go ::: coverage`
'   build-cli [--release] ......... build-cli (go install) · release ·
'                                     snapshot · hidden release-ledger
'   deploy-cli · dev-cli .......... deploy-cli (depends release, confirm,
'                                     wrangler deploy) · dev-cli (snapshot,
'                                     stage-cdn, wrangler dev)
'   stage-cdn ..................... hidden stage-cdn: go run ./internal/cdn/stage
'   build · deploy · test ......... build · deploy · test-defs: go run
'                                     ./internal/maintain/fleet <verb> <target>
'   e2e-full · idle · ladder ...... test-e2e-full · e2e-gated · idle-all ·
'                                     ladder-all · ladder:<def>
'   render-subagents .............. deleted (operator choice 3)
'   main.go dispatcher + gate.go .. deleted; verdicts are go test exit codes
'                                     and mise's failed-task list
'   ci (printf) ................... ci: depends on lint, build-check, test-go
'
' ── MEASURED ON mise 2026.10.17 (the lab, 2026-11-12) ──────────────────────
' * min_version = "2026.10.10" is accepted; `mise tasks validate` passes on
'   the full planned mise.toml (34 tasks).
' * Every run string, quoted or plain, runs under `sh -o errexit -c`: a Go
'   probe printed SHLVL=3, equal to a manual sh -c; no direct exec was seen.
' * An unset boolean usage flag renders "false", a passed one "true", and
'   {% if usage.x %} is false when unset.
' * usage refuses a bad choice, a missing required arg, an extra word and an
'   unknown flag; --help lists choices and defaults; flags may follow the arg.
' * Without a usage spec CLI args append to the last run entry; with one they
'   are consumed or refused.
' * { task = … } run entries run in order; a sub-task's tools reach it only.
' * A variadic arg rendered through {% for %} … | quote reaches argv as one
'   word per arg (`-run 'Test A'` arrived as two words).
' * [vars] rejects arrays; a backslash-continued """ string yields one regex.
' * skip_if renders Tera; the envflag word list skips on 1, true, YES, ' on ',
'   enable, enabled and runs on '', 0, false, no, 2 or unset.
' * `mise run --continue-on-error a ::: b ::: c` with wait_for runs in order
'   past a red task and exits 1 naming it; --jobs=1 keeps the CLI order.
' * Task env beats mise's GOBIN; GOBIN = false unsets it.
' * exec() in a template runs with the caller's PATH, not the task's tools.
' * confirm with no TTY fails ("pass --yes"); --yes and MISE_YES=1 pass; an
'   empty rendered confirm still prompts.
' * `mise run -n` prints rendered run lines, depends and sub-tasks, but no
'   env; `mise tasks info` prints env templates and run lines.
' * `mise generate git-pre-commit --write` writes a #!/bin/sh hook that execs
'   `mise run <task>`; in a linked worktree it writes the common .git/hooks,
'   and a worktree commit fires it.
' * go install and go build stamp vcs.revision and vcs.modified; go run
'   stamps neither.
' * A goreleaser snapshot's dist/metadata.json version equals the binary's
'   --version (0.1.6-SNAPSHOT-7a0c8cf4), and artifacts.json carries each CDN
'   binary's sha256.
' * covdata percent and textfmt read cov/unit directly.
' * Before the e2e gates changed, TestSandboxLadder and the idle check SKIPPED
'   with exit 0 on a host without docker or sbx.
' * get_env(name=X, default=D) yields "" for X= and D only when X is unset, so
'   `PROVEO_TEST_GO_TIMEOUT= mise run -n test-go-e2e` once printed a bare
'   -timeout. The {% set %} … | trim form yields the fallback for unset, "" and
'   "  ", in a run string and in an env value.
' * `| quote` wraps a string in '…' (-tag='x;echo INJECTED' stays one argv
'   word) and fails to render on a bool.
' * `mise run -n` checks confirm: without a TTY it exits 1; `-n --yes` prints
'   the plan and runs no depends and no run entry.
' * A go env file's GOBIN beats task env GOBIN = false.
'
' ── THE HOST SHELL THAT REMAINS ────────────────────────────────────────────
'   apps/cli/public/cli/install.sh, uninstall.sh   bootstrap before proveo
'                                                   exists; guarded bash
'   .git/hooks/post-commit                          mise's generated #!/bin/sh,
'                                                   untracked
'   the `sh -o errexit -c` hop                      around every plain-argv
'                                                   run string
' TestMiseTasksRunNoShellScripts holds the run strings to plain argv: an
' allowlist of bytes outside '…' and Tera blocks, each Tera value one quoted
' operand (a variable or one ( … ) group piped last through quote, since a
' filter binds tighter than ~), no leading assignment, no bash keyword,
' builtin or env first, no shell interpreter in any word, no non-ASCII, and
' only [tasks.<name>] tables with keys the scan reads.
'
' ── WHAT A MAINTAINER NOTICES ──────────────────────────────────────────────
' * `mise run lint` gates gofmt on every tracked .go file and lints e2e/.
' * baseline skips its 16 listed tests by name: no "passes here" note and no
'   per-package scope; go test flags pass after --.
' * coverage reads cov/unit; PROVEO_COV_DIR, PROVEO_CDN_ROOT, PROVEO_DIST_DIR
'   and PROVEO_CDN_REQUIRE_DIST are gone; PROVEO_VERSION is installer-only.
' * `mise run release` (tagged HEAD) and `mise run snapshot` replace
'   `build-cli -- --release`; dev-cli and test-images snapshot first (~25s).
' * build, deploy and test-defs need a target; the TTY picker is gone, and
'   choiceui FilterList takes one row.
' * idle-all and ladder-all report through go test -v and mise's failed-task
'   list instead of verdict tables.
' * Each ladder:<def> runs -run=^TestSandboxLadder$, where HEAD ran -run Ladder.
'   TestLadderReportNamesTheFirstFailure, TestLadderReportSendsRungZeroUpstream,
'   TestLadderReportSaysWhenNothingBroke and
'   TestLadderPromptIsEmptyUntilAnOperatorNamesOne leave ladder-all; they still
'   run in test-e2e and e2e-gated.
' * build, deploy and test-defs pass --tag and the target as one quoted word,
'   and -no-cache and -print only when set; `mise run -n build` shows that line.
' * `mise run -n deploy-cli` exits 1 at the confirm without a TTY; `mise run -n
'   --yes deploy-cli` prints the plan. A "no" at the confirm comes after
'   release ran, so dist/ and apps/cli/public/cli stay restaged
'   (apps/cli/README.md). HEAD's deploy-cli asked nothing.
' * deploy-cli runs TestStagedCDNIsTheTaggedRelease before wrangler, so
'   `--skip-deps` cannot publish a snapshot stage (_spec/_devops/release-gate.puml).
' * `mise run ci --no-race` forwards --no-race to test-go; ci runs
'   `mise run lint ::: build-check ::: test-go`, where it held three depends.
' * A host with `go env -w GOBIN=…` gets build-cli's binaries in that GOBIN.
'
' ── RISKS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' * A skip inside an opted-in gate fails only because failSkipsWhenOptedIn is
'   the first statement; TestOptedInE2EGatesFailTheirSkips pins its place.
' * e2e-gated sets PROVEO_IDLE_TEST=1 for the whole e2e pass, so its default
'   claudecode idle check fails without sbx instead of skipping.
' * A stale baseline row stays silent until someone reads test-go.
' * A host without cgo fails test-go, baseline and ci until --no-race.
' * The usage choices copy maintain.Registry;
'   TestImageTasksChoicesMatchTheRegistry pins them.
' * [Unverified] mise's aqua download of goreleaser 2.17.0 was not exercised.
'   test-images (and test-e2e, test-e2e-full) now snapshot first, so the
'   in-sandbox step 4 of _spec/_devops/release-gate.puml needs that download
'   through the sandbox's egress; HEAD needed only go there.
' * [Unverified] A real build, deploy or test-defs through the fleet main
'   (not --print) was not run.
' * The installed .git/hooks/post-commit still execs the deleted dispatcher
'   until the operator runs `mise run install-git-hooks` once; every commit
'   prints a go run error until then. CONTRIBUTING.md names the step.

component "mise.toml\nplain-argv tasks" as MISE <<app>>
component "go test gates\ninternal/contract · e2e" as GATES <<app>>
component "internal/cdn/stage\npackage main" as STAGE <<app>>
component "internal/maintain/fleet\npackage main" as FLEET <<app>>
component "goreleaser 2.17.0\nsnapshot · release" as GR <<app>>
cloud "wrangler\nproveo.ca/cli" as WR <<cloud>>
component "mise generate git-pre-commit\nuntracked .git/hooks/post-commit" as HOOK <<app>>
component "cmd/proveo-dev\nDELETED 2026-11-12" as GONE <<error>>

MISE ARROW_MAIN GATES : lint · baseline · test-go\nrelease-ledger · idle · ladder
MISE ARROW_MAIN GR : snapshot · release
GR ARROW_MAIN STAGE : dist/ metadata
MISE ARROW_MAIN STAGE : stage-cdn
MISE ARROW_MAIN FLEET : build · deploy · test-defs
MISE ARROW_CLOUD WR : deploy-cli · dev-cli
MISE ARROW_MAIN HOOK : install-git-hooks
HOOK ARROW_OPTIONAL MISE : mise run post-commit
GONE ARROW_ERROR MISE : replaced by

note right of GATES
  **The exit code is the verdict.** A gate is
  a Go test, so mise composes it like a task.
  An opted-in skip fails at cleanup.
end note

note bottom of STAGE
  **It trusts goreleaser's metadata.** It reads
  dist/artifacts.json and metadata.json and
  checks every sha256 before it writes.
end note

note bottom of FLEET
  **One main for three verbs.** mise checks the
  target first; --print shows the wave plan,
  which mise run -n cannot.
end note

note right of GR
  **Pinned per task, not in [tools].** Only
  snapshot and release resolve it, so fmt,
  lint and post-commit never fetch it.
end note

note bottom of WR
  **Only a tag reaches production.** deploy-cli
  refuses an untagged HEAD before goreleaser;
  dev-cli serves a local snapshot.
end note

note right of HOOK
  **The hook is mise's, and untracked.** It
  execs mise run post-commit, and
  SKIP_GIT_HOOKS still skips it via skip_if.
end note

note bottom of GONE
  **No dispatcher survives.** The cobra root,
  its 29 files and the shim are deleted. The
  name lives on in records like this one.
end note
@enduml
